WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
Kaze ni kami ga nabiku

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.150
My hair flows in the wind.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
Kokoro ni hirogaru aozora no deai

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.720
An encounter in the blue skies of our hearts...

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Tooku hanaretetemo

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.980
Though we are apart,

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
Kanjiru koto wa itsumo kimi dakara

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:21.590
I'm always thinking about you,

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
Itsu no hi ka mune wo hatte

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:26.930
so let's promise to meet again

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
Au koto wo yakusoku shiyou

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:32.410
one day, with our heads held high.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
Zutto futari owari no nai

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:39.020
We'll be together, like a dream

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
Yume wo egaku you ni

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:45.410
with no end.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
Kimi ni

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.440
I want

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
Kono omoi itsu no hi ka tsutaetai

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:56.400
to tell you this someday.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
Sabishisa wo shiawase ni kaeru tame

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:07.370
I'm right here next to you

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
to turn your loneliness into joy.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:16.460
Soba ni iru yo kokoro wa

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
I can feel your heart so close to mine.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:24.830
Konna ni chikaku ni kanjiru

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.080
Episode 21 - Flame Etude

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.760
And now we shall announce the contenders for the role of Helen Keller...

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:44.950
Auditions for The Miracle Worker

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:44.080
in <i>The Miracle Worker</i>.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.100
Rena Shiratori from the Kaze Troupe.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.000
Akiko Hayakawa, who has made several television appearances...

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.480
She represents the Tenma Troupe.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.890
Emi Kanaya, the most influential member of the One Star Academy's Acting Club.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:03.510
The next candidate needs no introduction:

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:06.360
Ayumi Himekawa from the Ondine Troupe.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.500
Our last contender is Maya Kitajima from the Tsukikage Acting Troupe.

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:16.010
Miss Kitajima?

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.090
Is Maya Kitajima present?

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.540
Miss Kitajima, is that you?

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.220
Pleased to meet you!

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.520
Ayumi!

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.690
She's always one step ahead of me. She's always above me.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:35.590
But winning the role of Helen is my last chance.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.630
And now, let me introduce the judges.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:41.140
Representing our very own company: Mr. Masumi Hayami.

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:45.130
Mr. Hajime Onodera, Ondine Troupe's Director.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:51.020
On the day of the audition, Utako Himekawa, who will be playing the role...

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.640
of Annie Sullivan, will also participate in the judging process.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:58.240
And just because Ayumi Himekawa happens to be Mrs. Himekawa's daughter,

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.260
she will receive no special treatment.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:03.520
Our judges will remain impartial throughout.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.970
Miss Ayumi. Is it true that you're not living with your mother anymore?

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:08.340
Yes, it's true.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.180
Why would you do such a thing when she's one of the judges as well as being your mother?

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:15.680
Exactly because I don't want people thinking it's like that!

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:20.610
I moved out so that I could be like every other contender!

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:25.340
I plan to win the role of Helen through skill alone.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.100
Completely independent of your relationship as mother and daughter?

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.300
Exactly.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.100
You can ask my mother. She will tell you the same.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.520
Excuse me.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.490
Hey, Utako Himekawa is here too!

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.760
It's a mother-daughter rivalry!

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:42.230
At nineteen months old, Helen Keller became deafblind.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.420
She met her tutor Annie Sullivan at the age of six.

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.430
Helen only has one line.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:54.640
At the very end of the play, she says "water".

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.640
When the water from the well trickles through her fingers,

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.610
Helen realizes that everything has a name.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:06.050
Helen. She couldn't see, hear, nor speak.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.210
How should I play her?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:16.590
"You need to improve your manners, Helen."

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:18.320
"Fold your napkin!"

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.800
"Fold it now!"

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.290
"You can't run away, Helen."

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:28.050
You've not finished eating yet!

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:30.820
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:32.310
Why did you turn around?

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:36.550
Maya, Helen's supposed to be deaf!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:42.980
Look, Princess Helen! It's your favorite doll.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.730
She's all the way over there!

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.190
Well? What are you doing?

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:51.530
Your doll's over there!

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:52.350
Yes.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:05.970
Stop right there, Maya.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:11.680
You were taking huge steps just now, weren't you?

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:13.790
Why were you doing that?

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:17.120
Because you were trying to avoid the shards, right?

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:21.140
Unconsciously, instinct told you to avoid hurting yourself.

00:05:21.140 --> 00:05:22.920
Because you can see.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:25.680
You're still using your eyes, Maya!

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:26.630
You're still using your ears!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.450
Right, let's start again from the beginning.

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:32.140
Now, fold the napkin on the table!

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:36.890
The second time Miss Sullivan appears...

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.880
That's not how you should be walking!

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:41.890
You're running away from Miss Sullivan whom you despise!

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:44.460
Ma'am!

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.180
You're looking for your mother!

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.710
Are you all right?

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:47.710
Maya!

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.850
I want you to go off by yourself and play as Helen.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:56.850
I have to play as Helen... when she can neither see nor hear.

00:05:56.850 --> 00:05:59.190
Ma'am, please. You need to take a rest.

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:02.120
If you keep going on like this, you're both going to collapse!

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:02.730
Silence!

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:04.350
She's right, you know.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.340
Perhaps you should take a break.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:13.170
I went to the hospital to see you but you weren't there.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:15.690
I know you're supposed to be released again soon, but you won't be...

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:17.510
if you're in this condition.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.660
That's none of your concern!

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.470
Why have you come here, anyway?

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:24.980
You don't know?

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:26.540
Today, this building...

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:33.090
...is being demolished. They're building apartments in its place.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:38.050
But we don't have anywhere else to rehearse!

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.260
Ma'am!

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.290
Ma'am! Hang in there!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.600
Ms. Tsukikage!

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:45.800
You bring nothing but bad luck!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.020
Nothing good ever happens when you're around!

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:50.730
Get out! Just get out!

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:01.480
Madam.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.260
A purple rose?

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.330
Look at this!

00:07:10.310 --> 00:07:12.340
It's an invitation!

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.300
It says:

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.840
If you desire it, you may use my summerhouse in Nagano to rehearse this summer.

00:07:18.520 --> 00:07:22.340
He says he won't be able to use it himself, but I'm free to go there whenever I like!

00:07:24.700 --> 00:07:28.350
Here's your mineral water!

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:30.100
Oh, thank you!

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.790
It's nice to have volunteers over the summer.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:38.330
You said it! All these people have come to help the deafblind children.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:40.650
They're doing a great job!

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:44.360
Isn't that... Ayumi Himekawa?

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.250
To make a role your own,

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:52.510
you must first completely absorb the character's reality.

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:59.020
Luckily, Helen was a real person, so there are plenty of books and pictures of her.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.600
But that's not enough.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:05.810
You have to recreate the real Helen with that as a basis.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.890
Are you Miss Maya Kitajima?

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.560
Yes!

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:42.180
If you need anything at all, make sure to let us know.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.720
That's right, Maya.

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:45.230
Yes, sir!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.610
It's so beautiful!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:03.840
It's from him!

00:09:03.840 --> 00:09:05.650
"Miss Maya Kitajima,

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:07.150
How are you?"

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:12.590
"Please use this house as you wish, either to rehearse or to relax."

00:09:12.590 --> 00:09:14.890
"I have only one condition."

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:18.510
"Please do not try to find out who I am."

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:21.990
"Is that all right? It is my only condition."

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.320
"From Your Fan," huh?

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.650
Thank you so much!

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:37.650
I'm going to use this place to get myself into the role of Helen!

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:45.670
Helen can't see nor hear.

00:09:46.090 --> 00:09:48.880
I wonder how she walked around the house in the woods...

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.550
where she lived with Miss Sullivan.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:04.950
It's so scary not being able to see!

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:11.150
Helen lost all sight and sound aged just nineteen months.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:15.570
She must have had to fumble around in a dark, silent world to get around.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:21.800
I wonder where Maya is.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:26.380
Maya, what happened to your clothes?!

00:10:26.380 --> 00:10:27.740
I'm back!

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:29.890
All that walking has made me hungry!

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.150
I'm going to change.

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.110
This looks healthy!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:38.980
Go ahead, dig in!

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.310
I wonder how Helen would eat.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:11:00.260
I apologize for my bad manners!

00:11:02.560 --> 00:11:04.450
I wonder if she's going to be okay.

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:06.470
She's certainly a strange one.

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:11.100
Right.

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:17.550
What's that doing here?

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.050
Helen would have stepped on the book.

00:11:21.230 --> 00:11:25.050
Instead, I tried to pick it up without thinking.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.410
What am I going to do?

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:30.100
At this rate, I'm never going to become Helen!

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:38.300
Please let us interview Miss Himekawa!

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:40.370
She's here, isn't she?

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:45.110
How can she use a place like this to do research for her acting?!

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.090
Excuse me, but that's not how it is!

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:50.170
Miss Himekawa is...

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.720
There she is!

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:55.640
Miss Himekawa, please talk to us!

00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:57.220
Don't you think all this is a bit immoral?

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:59.730
Don't you care that you're being a burden to these kind people?

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:09.020
I see. You're pretending to be the disabled Helen.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.000
Well, let's see...

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:16.230
What are you doing?!

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:24.060
Miss Ayumi is staying here as a deafblind person for the time being!

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:28.230
She came here because she wanted to learn what it's like...

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:30.000
not being able to see, hear or speak.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.210
She asked us to help her.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.610
Her interest is genuine!

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:41.270
It's more than obvious if you look at these children.

00:12:41.270 --> 00:12:44.760
So take your sensationalist crap elsewhere!

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.480
Please leave!

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:50.950
She fell over really easily, didn't she?

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.390
You think? You or I would have put out a hand to catch ourselves!

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:57.380
Well, if you couldn't see, you'd trip easily too, but...

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:01.380
She's a frightening actress, that one.

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:05.400
Ayumi Himekawa's a real genius.

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:15.910
No, I have to stop.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:18.750
I have to think about becoming Helen.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:24.670
But how can I capture her heart...

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:28.070
when she can't see nor hear?

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.000
That's it!

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:39.060
Maya!

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:42.390
She's not responding...

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:44.980
Maya?

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:49.520
What's wrong?

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:53.180
Maya!

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.360
Where are you going?

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:57.300
Maya! Maya!

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:59.300
She's not answering!

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:00.980
Maya!

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:07.230
Look! She's got earplugs in!

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.040
Maya!

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:13.850
It's Mr. and Mrs. Tsuda.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.820
It must be morning.

00:14:22.370 --> 00:14:28.040
P-l-e-a-s-e d-o-n-t w-o-r-r-y.

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:35.850
I'm rehearsing for a play.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:45.420
The wind.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:55.990
It's cold. Is it morning?

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:57.680
Or is it nighttime?

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.110
I'm scared.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.170
You're quite resourceful, Masumi.

00:16:03.170 --> 00:16:09.390
Daito throws this party every year and all the movers and shakers eat it up!

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:13.580
The Daito stars get free publicity and you get to rub elbows with society's finest.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:17.010
And the Daito Corporation grows even bigger.

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:19.090
I hope so.

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:20.940
You have a phone call.

00:16:20.940 --> 00:16:22.240
Who from? Tsuda?

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.140
Please excuse me.

00:16:24.610 --> 00:16:29.510
But you only see these guests as tools for your own advancement.

00:16:29.510 --> 00:16:34.180
Is there no one outside of work who you can socialize with...

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.490
like a normal human being?

00:16:36.410 --> 00:16:38.390
Goro, is that you?

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.880
It's Hayami.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:49.280
And I thought I was being extra-careful when I was coming down the stairs.

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.840
I can't take it anymore!

00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:55.990
I want to take off this bandage!

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.850
I want to talk to someone!

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:02.600
I can't stand groping around in this dark, silent world anymore!

00:17:02.860 --> 00:17:05.590
I don't care if I never get into Helen's head!

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.500
Ouch!

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:13.140
Who's this?

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:16.800
That's not Mr. Tsuda's hand!

00:17:17.690 --> 00:17:20.730
Who are you?

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:24.360
This scent...

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:30.780
Thorns.

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:49.240
Are... you... Mr... Purple...

00:17:49.240 --> 00:17:50.470
Roses?

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.360
It's him!

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:03.340
The man who's supported me ever since my debut!

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:07.970
I've finally met him!

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:12.140
Thank you! Thank you!

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:14.610
Little one...

00:18:25.550 --> 00:18:29.760
I'm a complete stranger to him, yet he's been so kind.

00:18:30.230 --> 00:18:33.290
I'm truly grateful.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.460
Wait!

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:38.260
Who are you?

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:41.260
Please! At least tell me your name!

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:44.520
You've helped me so much!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:50.890
Whenever I'm feeling down, I think of you, so please... tell me your name at least!

00:18:53.910 --> 00:19:07.650
I... am... really... looking... forward... to... your... Helen.

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:13.810
I'm going to do it! I won't quit!

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:19.420
What's wrong with me?

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:23.060
She's more than ten years younger than me...

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:25.550
To think that a man of my age...

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:33.500
Theater Club

00:19:30.180 --> 00:19:34.720
I'm studying the gestures of a real deafblind girl...

00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:38.650
This part where she shakes her head is very effective, but then...

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.320
Stop right there!

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:45.010
No, that facial expression is all wrong!

00:19:45.340 --> 00:19:48.510
Can you please record me one more time?

00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:56.280
Ayumi is really sticking to this, isn't she?

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:58.130
At the moment, she's playing.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:03.460
They can't hear, speak nor see, so deafblind children...

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:05.150
look inwards.

00:20:05.150 --> 00:20:09.020
I can't believe it. It's like she really can't see anymore!

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:10.840
Like she really can't hear anymore.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:13.360
Is she really just acting still?

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:18.240
You know, even knowing the situation, I sometimes have my doubts.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.460
She's frightening.

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:26.810
What's that girl doing?

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:29.870
She just keeps winding and unwinding that ball of string, over and over again.

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:31.740
She's having fun.

